(Haydock) — The most incompatible things are united. (Theodoret) — The sinner melts into tears at the sight of God’s judgments. (St. Augustine) — Stores, which are his will and decrees. (Theodoret) (Jeremias li. 16.)"],["haydock",14,null,"haydock","Entreated. Deuteronomy xxxii. 36. “Have pity,” (Berthier) or revenge."],["haydock",20,null,"haydock","Fear. It was important to distinguish the priests from the people. (Calmet)"]],"au":{"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"]}}